    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d611">

                <pb facs="1028" n="932" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg932"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.162/27: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-08-25T11:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 25,
                                1925—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:48
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>61. Draft of the treaty of friendship, commerce and consular rights was submitted
                    to the Foreign Office this morning.</p>
                <p>I should appreciate it if the Department could for my confidential guidance
                    telegraph briefly principal grounds on which most-favored-nation <pb facs="1029"
                        n="933" xml:id="pg933"/> treatment is desired to be used discreetly in
                    conversation without committing the Department in any way.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
